# Persistent Memory Rule

`MEMORY.md` at the repo root is long-term AI memory. Read it at the start of every session for context on known mistakes and patterns.

## After Every Correction

When you make a mistake and the user corrects you:

1. Add a row to `MEMORY.md` in this format:

   ```
   | YYYY-MM-DD | What went wrong | What to do instead |
   ```

2. Tell the user: "I've updated MEMORY.md so I won't make this mistake again."

## Rules

- Read `MEMORY.md` before starting any non-trivial task
- Update it immediately after any correction
- Edit entries ruthlessly — remove outdated rows, merge duplicates
- Treat it as authoritative: if MEMORY.md contradicts your training, MEMORY.md wins for this project

## Key Known Patterns (summary — see MEMORY.md for full list)

- Contracts: `.cursor/contracts/` (not `agents/contracts/`)
- Playbooks: `.cursor/playbooks/` (not `agents/playbooks/`)
- Validate command: `3lens validate all` (not `3lens validate contracts`)
- PR checklist: `.cursor/agents/code-reviewer.md` (not a separate file)
